WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.740
so there is a renewed and re-energized Beto
or war running around out there.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.070
He's running for the Democratic nomination
in 2020 it's not going super well Beto as

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.379
port polling two to 3% in his latest post.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:13.950
Second debate polls.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.360
His first debate performance was atrocious,
but Beto is on fire this week.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.830
I told you earlier this week that Beto was
finally speaking sort of more from the heart.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:26.550
He wasn't using these calculated talking points
and he was speaking earlier this week about

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:32.710
the El Paso shooting very clearly and very
precisely, drawing a connective, a line between

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:38.070
Donald Trump's rhetoric and the shooting and
now he straight up called Donald Trump a white

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.410
supremacist on live television.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.410
Take a look at this clip.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:42.410
Okay.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.880
You've been very clear that you believe the
president is a racist.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.180
Is the president a white supremacist?

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.190
He is.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.800
He's also made that very clear.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.620
He's dehumanized or sought to do dehumanize
those who do not look like or pray like the

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.000
majority here in this country.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.280
He said, I wished we had more immigrants from
Nordic countries because those from Haiti

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.420
bring aids, those from Africa come from shithole
nations.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.670
Um, he's been very clear about who he prefers
to be in this country and who he literally

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:13.680
wants to keep out with walls and cages and
militarization and torture and cruelty.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.380
And again, we in El Paso had borne the brunt
of all of that, but we in El Paso are standing

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.810
up to all of that right now.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:22.860
And I've never been more proud of this community
than I am at this moment.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:26.520
I don't really know if Trump is a white supremacist.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.230
He's certainly fomenting and coalescing and
encouraging white supremacy.

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.380
But this is a great new Beto.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.850
I set it Monday and I'll repeat it today.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:39.180
If this had been the better we'd been seeing
all along, he might be polling better than

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.180
two or 3%.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:45.600
I mean, it's really a breath of fresh air
in a world riddled with calculated talking

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.490
points and hedging on everything.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:51.130
And from what I understand, there are people
around Beto.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:55.700
I don't know if official campaign people or
just people that he talks to who are cautioning

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:58.150
him about saying certain things.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:04.119
So bluntly politicians are supposed to you
know, have caveats and speak in vague language

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:10.450
that failed Beto completely the calculated
milk toast bullet points have completely failed

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:15.760
him and left him in a losing position in this
primary, it's probably too late already to

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.480
actually help them recover but maybe not.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.870
He has qualified for the third debate.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:26.670
The tell it like it is version of Beto is
absolutely the way to go and in fact this

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:33.130
is the version of Beto that almost saw him
take out an incumbent Republican senator in

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.120
the Red State of Texas, Ted Cruz.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:41.440
He ultimately did lose but not by much and
it was close because it was genuine.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:47.150
Tell it like it is, say what's on your mind
Beto and it's really just kind of sad that

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.959
telling it like it is in normal speech.

00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:52.920
Is this notable for a politician?

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.470
Beto was asked a question, he answered it
clearly with a yes or no.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:03.050
He supported it with examples and you can
say, well, it's easier now for Beto to just

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:07.370
let it fly and to behave this way because
he no longer has anything to lose because

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:11.920
he's pulling 2% you may be right about what
has inspired the change.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.310
Maybe it is that he feels like he has nothing
else to lose.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:18.910
It could just be that he is genuinely affected
by what's been going on in El Paso because

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:24.160
that is where he's from, but it's a sad commentary
on the political environment either way, whatever

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.160
the reasons are.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:30.560
I'm glad to see this Beto and by the way,
whatever you think about white supremacist

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:35.349
as a term for Donald Trump, corporate media
won't even call Trump a liar.

00:03:35.349 --> 00:03:37.280
We've talked about this before.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:44.050
Corporate media will say when Trump has strayed
from the facts, when Trump has not been accurate

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:49.400
in the things that he has said times the president
didn't tell the whole truth.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:55.000
And from what I understand, there are legal
reasons why many corporate media outlets stopped

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.540
short of just straight up calling Donald Trump
a liar.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:04.379
But it would really be great if it wasn't
so rare to just call things what they are.

00:04:04.379 --> 00:04:08.800
And I'm actually, I'm not, you know, people
know that my politics are more in line with

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.830
Bernie's, uh, or with Elizabeth Warren's for
example.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:16.699
Um, not necessarily Beto O'Rourke, but I hope
that this Beto continues.

00:04:16.699 --> 00:04:22.330
I hope that this is the better that we see
in the September 12th or 12th and 13th debates.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:26.229
I guess depending on how many people are left
in the race at that point in time because

00:04:26.229 --> 00:04:32.330
this actually is a Beto that might inspire
rather than confuse and sort of just, uh,

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:35.520
make people wonder what is it that he even
really stands for.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.749
It feels too calculated.

00:04:36.749 --> 00:04:39.650
It feels to focus grouped in some way.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:40.990
Let's hope that it continues.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:47.409
And, uh, by the way, speaking of a politician,
just speaking from the heart and telling it

00:04:47.409 --> 00:04:54.139
like it is, uh, I was able to watch more of
Bernie's appearance on the Joe Rogan experience

00:04:54.139 --> 00:04:55.139
yesterday.

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:58.800
A bunch of people on my twitch stream yesterday
said, you really got to check it out.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:04:59.999
It was really good.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:00.999
And I know that.

00:05:00.999 --> 00:05:05.410
So, so there's this like never ending battle,
not to go completely off script here proverbially.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:11.430
Um, uh, but there's this never ending battle
about should the left appear on Joe Rogan's

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:16.339
show because he allows so many right-wing
talking points to be parroted uninterrupted

00:05:16.339 --> 00:05:19.289
or should left this avoid Joe Rogan's show.

00:05:19.289 --> 00:05:21.430
I think the answer is very clear.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:26.379
Anybody who goes on Joe Rogan's program is
going to be giving an opera, given an opportunity

00:05:26.379 --> 00:05:32.499
to sort of flesh out their ideas with only
mild resistance or pushback from Joe.

00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:33.719
Like that's the format.

00:05:33.719 --> 00:05:37.220
And he pushed back on things I said a little
bit when I was on his program back in June.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:42.279
Um, and he pushed back a little bit with Bernie,
but what was fantastic about Bernie's appearance,

00:05:42.279 --> 00:05:46.150
which was only I think like 50 or 67 minutes
long or something like that.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:52.259
What was great about it is that Joe provided,
you could argue that it was not enough or

00:05:52.259 --> 00:05:56.889
too much depending on your politics, but he
provided an amount of pushback to Bernie that

00:05:56.889 --> 00:06:01.969
was enough of for Bernie to be able to come
right back with counterpoints.

00:06:01.969 --> 00:06:07.620
That in that environment were very, very strong,
fantastic appearance for Bernie Sanders on

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:08.699
the program.

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:13.530
I don't know if it's you know enough to move
polling for Bernie, but it certainly enough

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:18.400
to generate donations for Bernie, which unfortunately
in the money in politics, status quo system

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.439
that we have makes a difference.

00:06:20.439 --> 00:06:21.949
And I think it was completely worthwhile for
Bernie to do it.

